// H96 Max V58: NetworkManager's default "Wired connection 1" profile leaves IPv6
// nominally enabled on eth0 (net.ipv6.conf.eth0.disable_ipv6=0) even though this
// LAN has no working IPv6 route out — confirmed live: `curl -6` to a real Ubuntu
// mirror fails outright (exit 7, no route), `curl -4` to the same mirror succeeds
// instantly. The earlier `noipv6` fix in /etc/dhcpcd.conf ([V3.2.2]) only ever
// covered the standalone wpa_supplicant/dhcpcd path used for wlan0 — it never
// touched Ethernet, which NetworkManager manages independently.
//
// Confirmed live this let apt/PackageKit acquire attempts intermittently try the
// dead IPv6 path and fail: one heavy install (kdenlive + ~70 deps) succeeded by
// silently falling back to IPv4, then the very next install attempt, seconds
// later, failed immediately with PackageKit::Transaction::ErrorNoNetwork
// ("No network connection available") — reported by Discover as a connectivity
// problem despite the box having full, working internet the entire time
// (nmcli reported "full" connectivity throughout; the polkit auth for that same
// failed transaction succeeded).
//
// Forcing apt to IPv4-only removes the dead path entirely rather than trying to
// fix NetworkManager's per-connection IPv6 defaults (broader, riskier change for
// a bug that is specific to package acquisition).
Acquire::ForceIPv4 "true";
